This is typically an error message caused by attempting to dump from an
Digital Unix computer to some other brand which uses a different 'rmt'
program (which is used by rdump).

It can also be caused by a bad 'dot' file such as a .cshrc
which outputs some unexpected characters when it is run on the
tape-drive machine for the 'rmt' process.
You should do rsh <tape-machine> date and verify that ONLY the date is
displayed.

I suggest you avoid rdump because it is 2-4 times slower than a 'dump
pipe' something like

dump <arguments> - /partition  | rsh tape-machine dd bs=3Dblocksize
of=3D<tapedev>

It also avoids such incompatibilities (Digital Unix is the only REAL
offender that I know of.  Several of its rmt internal commands (see 'man
rmt') conflict with commonly used commands on other architectures' rmt
such as Sun and SGI. Digital Unix uses one of these conflicting commands
to rewind the tape or maybe detect Digital Unix at the other end (I don't
remember).


