Subject: SUMMARY: install of SSRT0588U renders the system unusable?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079036515844


My Original Question Was:

> Has anyone on this list installed the SSRT0588U security patch that
> is suppost to correct the problems in the 'edauth' command, as well
> as other programs which use the security libraries?
> 
> When we try to install it and then attempt to log in to the system,
> we get the message about 'last successful login', but then the
> login process disconnects.  We've also tried rebooting, but then
> we had to crash the system to get back in and replace the old
> shared library to make it work again.
>

The Answer Is: 

It turns out that, for SSRT0588U to operate correctly, you must have
already installed patch kit #3 on your system, at least under DU 4.0d,
but probably under all the operating systems.

Once I installed #3 and then installed the edauth fix, everything 
works correctly.  This little item was apparently left out of the
documentation for SSRT0588U.

