Subject: Possible bug with restore in 4.0E
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079036515678

I upgraded to 4.0E this weekend and what a nightmare.  
First of all the tape devices are missing if you boot from 
the cd and take the Unix Shell option. I had to reconfigure 
my root disk and had to boot from cd.  The upgrade to 4.0E 
was pretty simple otherwise.  Finally figured out you can 
do a MAKEDEV tz(x) and it will make all the devices for you.

Then the big one came.  Once i repartitioned the drive, I 
began to reload the disk from backup.  I have been 
accustomed to using restore -i (interactive option) and 
issuing the add command which will add everything in the 
file system and then doing an extract.  Well I couldnt 
login after doing this.  I had no shell.  I could get a 
login prompt but never get logged in.  I re-loaded the data 
several times but the same results.  I finally 
figured out that the /usr/bin/sh among other files 
were not being restored.  Finally I decided to use restore 
-rv and everything worked great.  So I guess there is 
either a bug in the interactive mode or there is a limit on 
the number of files it is able to mark and extract.  Just 
thought I would pass this along in case someone else 
stumbles across it as well.

----------------------
