The answer for this problem was solved by friendly DEC support member.
Unfortunatly there isn't a fix for it currently.
DEC's write buffer is maximum at 8k.
Solaris's write buffer defaults to 32k.
This is why the Solaris implemenation seemed so much faster.

When Solaris wsize is moved down to 8k, its timings are similar to the DECs.

I have been told that Engineers are currently working on providing a larger
wsize in future releases of Digital UNX.
		-grant


