From: John Francini <francini@nashua.progress.com>

A couple of things here...

"skip=1" says to skip one record, not one file, at least according to the dd
man page.

I think you may have to actually make a script that skips a file (using mt
rather than dd to do the skip), then loops 10 times doing:

	dd to read a file and write it to the second tape
	mt eof (to write an end-of-file mark, since I think dd is too dumb
                to do so)

At the end of the whole set of 10, use mt eof a second time to write a logical
EOT (two or more tape marks in a row).

Of course, all this is done with the norewind device names.

If someone else comes up with a more elegant solution, I'd be pleased to be
corrected!

Thanks,

