jrobens@davidjones.com.au


There was no magic answer unfortunately.

The simple answer is to mirror up the volumes before adding them to ASE.
I had actually considered this, but..., our change management people
dont like ANYTHING much being done on a LIVE server unless it is being
done in a scheduled maintenance slot (almost always at weekends).  I was
seeking a FAST way of doing it in a maintenance slot.


(I am not particularly an HP fan, but the HP-LVM mirroring does seem to
be better than LSM in this respect...

If you LVCREATE a volume to its full (big) size, then LVEXTEND it by
adding (a second) mirror, LVDISPLAY shows the volume mirrors synching
up.  This takes - well as long as it takes- just as LSM does.

However, if you LVCREATE it small (say 4mb), then LVEXTEND it by adding
(a second) mirror, LVDISPLAY shows the volume mirrors synching up, but
they sync up (obviously) very quickly - just as LSM does.  However, if
you then LVEXTEND the (small mirrored) volume to its required (big)
size, the extension is almost instantaneous.  LVDISPLAY shows both
mirrors are synced up and there is no mirror activity so far as I can
see.

I can only guess that there is some inteligence here which says 'ah -
I'm extending both mirrors simultaneously by the same amount so I dont
need to do any shadow copies'.)


The original posting is at the end of this document


