Subject: SUMMARY: Problem printing with enscript
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079036515452

Well, I solved the problem.  (and yes I do feel like an idiot)

It turns out, the problem was with the queue.  We were routing the output
of the Alpha through a Windows NT server queue.  This was essentially
desirable as it reduced management of multiple queues.  Well, the NT queue
does _something_ to the job that causes the printer to hate it (thus
printing reams of PS codes).  One more reason to curse M$ to the end of the
Earth.  Fixed the DU queue to print directly to the JetDirect card, and
voila!  Nice output.

Now to set this up as a filter.  I'm off to give it a stab.

Thanks all!
Jon

